A||N||2||87ECO5||Spring Swap||||5||
Z||000000||87ECO5||06-05-2000||09:31 AM||||I've got an '87 economy coupe and an '84 SE parts car.  I've heard that the economy coupes had softer springs than the other models.<P>So, my question is, can I pull the springs from the '84 SE and install them in my economy coupe?  Will they fit?  Will I need to make any other changes or modifications (different shocks/struts, other suspension mods/changes, etc.)?<P>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||06-05-2000||10:39 AM||||Yes, You can swap the springs. There is only a 25lbs per inch difference from 84 SE to 87 coupe springs. For future reference:<BR>84-87 coupe is 250 lbs per inch<BR>84-87 SE/85 GT is 275 lbs per inch<BR>86-87 GT is 285 lbs per inch.<BR>I was never able to comfirm if 88 spring rates were the same or not.<BR>You can just change the springs but you may also want to change the sway bar too. it is slightly bigger on the SE. everything else is the same.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 06-05-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||87ECO5||06-06-2000||07:50 AM||||Thanks, Oreif!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
